## 1. Core Java Mastery

> The differentiator between a mid-level and senior engineer is depth here. You must reason about *how* the JVM behaves under load, not just *what* the API does.

### ? Beginner Refresh (? 1–2 weeks)
- **Collections Deep Dive** — internal structure of `HashMap` (buckets, treeification at 8 entries, resize/rehash), `ArrayList` vs `LinkedList`, `ConcurrentHashMap` lock striping, `CopyOnWriteArrayList`, `TreeMap` (red-black tree). Know Big-O and when each wins.
- **Java 8 features** — lambdas, `Stream` API, `Optional`, method references, functional interfaces, default methods.
- ? Rewrite a legacy imperative data-processing class using Streams; benchmark before/after.

### ? Intermediate (? 3–4 weeks)
- **Multithreading & Concurrency** — `synchronized`, `volatile`, `happens-before`, Java Memory Model, `Atomic*` classes, `ReentrantLock`, `ReadWriteLock`, `CountDownLatch`, `Semaphore`, `CyclicBarrier`.
- **Executor Framework** — `ThreadPoolExecutor` internals (core/max pool, queue types, rejection policies), `ScheduledExecutorService`, sizing thread pools correctly.
- **CompletableFuture** — composition (`thenApply`, `thenCompose`, `thenCombine`), exception handling (`exceptionally`, `handle`), custom executors, avoiding common blocking pitfalls.
- **Java 11 & 17 features** — `var`, HTTP Client, records, sealed classes, pattern matching, switch expressions, text blocks.
- ? Build a bounded producer-consumer pipeline; then rebuild it with `CompletableFuture` + a custom pool.

### ? Advanced (? 4–6 weeks)
- **JVM Internals** — class loading (bootstrap/platform/application loaders), bytecode, JIT (C1/C2, tiered compilation), escape analysis, method inlining, runtime data areas.
- **Memory Management** — heap layout (young/old gen, Eden/Survivor), metaspace, stack vs heap, off-heap memory, memory leaks vs retention, `WeakReference`/`SoftReference`/`PhantomReference`.
- **Garbage Collection** — G1 (default), ZGC, Shenandoah, Parallel GC; how to read GC logs, pause-time goals, tuning flags (`-Xmx`, `-XX:MaxGCPauseMillis`).
- **Design Patterns** — GoF (Strategy, Factory, Builder, Observer, Decorator, Proxy, Template Method), plus enterprise patterns (Repository, Unit of Work, DTO, Facade). Recognize them inside Spring.
- ? Profile a memory leak with **VisualVM / JFR / async-profiler**; capture and interpret a heap dump in **Eclipse MAT**.

### ? Expert (? ongoing)
- **Latest Java features (21+)** — virtual threads (Project Loom), structured concurrency, scoped values, pattern matching for switch, sequenced collections. Understand when virtual threads replace reactive stacks.
- Set team-wide concurrency guidelines and JVM tuning baselines for production services.
- ? Migrate a thread-pool-bound service to virtual threads; measure throughput and tail latency changes.

